<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Drawing coloured balls from a bag without replacement</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>A bag contains {@num_R@} red (R) balls and {@num_B@} blue (B) balls. Two balls are drawn one at a time <b>without replacement</b>.</p>
<p>Draw a tree diagram to show all the possible outcomes, and use it to answer the questions. Give each answer as a fraction.</p>
<p><b>a) </b> Find the probability that both balls are red.</p>
<div>\(P(\text{both red}) =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>
<p><b>b) </b> Find the probability that exactly one ball is red.</p>
<div>\(P(\text{exactly one red}) =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>
<p><b>c) </b> Find the probability that at least one ball is blue.</p>
<div>\(P(\text{at least one blue}) =\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>On a <strong>tree diagram</strong> each branch carries the probability of that outcome, and we <strong>multiply along a path</strong> to get the probability of that sequence. Because the first ball is <em>not replaced</em>, the second-stage probabilities depend on what was drawn first: there is one ball fewer, and one fewer of the colour already drawn.</p>
<div style="text-align:center;" role="img" aria-label="Tree diagram for two draws without replacement, with branch and path probabilities.">
[[jsxgraph width="460px" height="182px"]]
(function() {
  var L1 = [['R', '{#pR1#}'],['B', '{#pB1#}']], L2 = [[['R', '{#pRgR#}'],['B', '{#pBgR#}']],[['R', '{#pRgB#}'],['B', '{#pBgB#}']]], LV = ['RR: {#pRR#}','RB: {#pRB#}','BR: {#pBR#}','BB: {#pBB#}'];
  var n = 4, wide = LV.length ? 15 : 12;
  var b = JXG.JSXGraph.initBoard(divid, {boundingbox:[-0.4, n + 0.4, wide, 0.3], axis:false, grid:false,
      showNavigation:false, showCopyright:false, pan:{enabled:false}, zoom:{enabled:false}});
  function lab(p, q, t, txt) {
    // t: how far along the branch the label sits
    // probability label 55% along the branch, above an upward branch and below a downward one
    var x = p[0] + t*(q[0]-p[0]), y = p[1] + t*(q[1]-p[1]);
    var off = (q[1] >= p[1]) ? 0.32 : -0.32;
    b.create('text', [x, y + off, txt], {anchorX:'middle', anchorY:'middle', fontSize:13, fixed:true, strokeColor:'#1565c0'});
  }
  var y = n, k = 0, root = [0, (n + 1)/2];
  b.create('point', root, {name:'', size:3, fixed:true, color:'#333', showInfobox:false});
  for (var i = 0; i < L1.length; i++) {
    var m = L2[i].length, ymid = y - (m - 1)/2, p1 = [3.0, ymid];
    b.create('segment', [root, p1], {strokeColor:'#555', fixed:true});
    lab(root, p1, 0.55, L1[i][1]);
    b.create('text', [3.15, ymid, L1[i][0]], {anchorY:'middle', fontSize:15, fixed:true});
    for (var j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      var s2 = [6.3, ymid], p2 = [9.2, y];
      b.create('segment', [s2, p2], {strokeColor:'#555', fixed:true});
      lab(s2, p2, 0.72, L2[i][j][1]);
      b.create('text', [9.35, y, L2[i][j][0]], {anchorY:'middle', fontSize:15, fixed:true});
      if (LV.length) b.create('text', [12.0, y, LV[k]], {anchorY:'middle', fontSize:13, fixed:true, strokeColor:'#2e7d32'});
      y -= 1; k++;
    }
  }
})();
[[/jsxgraph]]
</div>
<p><b>a)</b> Both red is the single path R then R: \(P(RR) = {@pR1@} \times {@pRgR@} = {@pRR@}\).</p>
<p><b>b)</b> Exactly one red happens on <em>two</em> paths, RB and BR, so we add them: \(P(RB) + P(BR) = {@pRB@} + {@pBR@} = {@ta2@}\).</p>
<p><b>c)</b> "At least one blue" is every outcome except RR, so by the <strong>complement rule</strong> \(P = 1 - P(RR) = 1 - {@pRR@} = {@ta3@}\).</p>
<p>Check: the four path probabilities add up to 1.</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2026063000</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[num_R : rand([3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]);
num_B : rand([2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]);
T : num_R + num_B;
/* branch probabilities */
pR1 : num_R/T;  pB1 : num_B/T;
pRgR : (num_R-1)/(T-1);  pBgR : num_B/(T-1);
pRgB : num_R/(T-1);      pBgB : (num_B-1)/(T-1);
/* path probabilities */
pRR : pR1*pRgR;  pRB : pR1*pBgR;  pBR : pB1*pRgB;  pBB : pB1*pBgB;
ta1 : pRR;
ta2 : pRB + pBR;
ta3 : 1 - pRR;
/* Misconceptions */
w1_repl : (num_R/T)^2;                 /* drew with replacement */
w2_one  : pRB;                         /* only one of the two paths */
w2_repl : 2*num_R*num_B/T^2;           /* both paths, but with replacement */
w3_bb   : pBB;                         /* "both blue" instead of "at least one blue" */
w3_repl : 1 - (num_R/T)^2;             /* complement, but with replacement */]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
